gaLP(){return"Our manifesto"},
gaLQ(){return"A sense of purpose gives life meaning.\n\nLiving on autopilot isn't living: we choose to move through life with awareness.\n\nLife is better shared.\n\nOur circles are the network that holds us up.\n\nAsking for help is an act of courage.\n\nFor the hard days, a strategy.\n\nKnowing ourselves is where it all begins."},
gaLR(){return"Your North"},
gaLS(){return"Having a North doesn't guarantee you'll live the way you want: detours and surprises will always show up. But not having one guarantees you won't live it.\n\nYour North is the compass that brings you back to center when the path gets blurry. Not a fixed destination: a direction you choose every day.\n\nDefining it means taking the wheel: every step stops being random and points toward something that's yours.\n\nSo that ten years from now, life hasn't slipped through your fingers."},
gaLK(){return"Metriotes"},
gaLL(){return"Metriotes comes from the Greek \u03bc\u03b5\u03c4\u03c1\u03b9\u03cc\u03c4\u03b7\u03c2: balance, the right measure. Not a lukewarm average, but a choice: to live in balance, not in the extremes.\n\nLiving in balance starts by looking at what usually stays invisible: the behaviors we repeat without noticing, the emotions we feel without naming, and what triggers them.\n\nMetriotes exists to make conscious what you can't see today, so you stop reacting on autopilot.\n\nBecause only when you see what you couldn't see before can you decide how you want to live."},
